==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage plays similarly to the original Ch.1 Andromeda, albeit with a Dread Bore and Ginger Snache being Zombified into Znache and a Cat Limit Restriction. Units like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] are great at dealing with Dread Bore, and the latter has great DPS. Seafarer, as usual, deals with Nimoy Bore very well.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
While the enemy variety has been reduced greatly, your cat limit has too, from 15 to 10 compared to Chapter 1. It is very crucial to spawn units appropriately and not spawn units haphazardly, as the Cat Limit can prevent you from sending out your stronger units sooner. [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] is great here, as it can resurface Zang Roo and deal hefty percentage damage to her when she buries under your frontline.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
A true pain of a stage, the massive variety of enemy traits means you're likely to rely on generalists rather than specialists. The main threats in this stage are Cadaver Bear, Spacefish Jones, and Ragin' Gory. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] destroys the Ragin' Gories, and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong]] can easily stall out Cadaver, and a [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime]] wave or 2 can easily dispatch the eel brothers, though watch out for Spacefish. J.J. Jackrabbit and Gabriel are the main peons you should watch out for, with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] being a great help against Jackrabbit particularly while also damaging gories very well thanks to his Behemoth Slayer ability.

